WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.093 --> 00:00:07.754
Roscoe poked around in the pot with a fork.

2
00:00:07.755 --> 00:00:14.635
"There! I got it!" He lifted his soggy handkerchief and squeezed it out over the pot.

3
00:00:14.636 --> 00:00:20.469
Oh boy! That sheriff was a terrible cook!

4
00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:22.822
The soup started bubbling.

5
00:00:22.823 --> 00:00:27.441
Roscoe grabbed a spoon and tasted it.

6
00:00:27.442 --> 00:00:32.553
"Pretty bland," he said. "It needs salt and pepper."

7
00:00:32.554 --> 00:00:37.673
He sprinkled in some salt. Then he reached for the pepper shaker.

8
00:00:37.674 --> 00:00:41.708
As he shook the pepper shaker, the top fell off.

9
00:00:41.709 --> 00:00:45.013
Pepper poured into the pot.

10
00:00:45.014 --> 00:00:50.726
Roscoe gulped. "Uh-oh, that's way too much!"

11
00:00:50.727 --> 00:00:55.168
Roscoe scooped out the top of the pepper shaker.

12
00:00:55.169 --> 00:00:58.691
"I don't want Miss Annie to take a bite of that."

13
00:00:58.692 --> 00:01:01.895
The sheriff stared into the pot.

14
00:01:01.896 --> 00:01:06.823
A huge blob of black pepper floated in the soup.

15
00:01:06.824 --> 00:01:15.750
"Maybe she won't taste it if I mix it in." Roscoe stirred and stirred.

16
00:01:15.751 --> 00:01:21.244
Finally he covered the pot and took it off the stove.

17
00:01:21.245 --> 00:01:26.550
He wrapped a towel around it and grabbed a bowl and spoon.

18
00:01:26.551 --> 00:01:33.559
But . . . hmm. How could he carry the pot and the bowl?

19
00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:36.282
He took off his cowboy hat.

20
00:01:36.283 --> 00:01:39.759
He put the bowl on his head like a cap.

21
00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:45.824
Roscoe grinned. "Miss Annie will be so pleased!"

22
00:01:45.825 --> 00:01:50.324
At the schoolhouse the students weren't doing much work.

23
00:01:50.325 --> 00:01:57.356
Instead they were listening to Cleo's stories about being a deputy.

24
00:01:57.357 --> 00:02:02.629
"I told you Deputy Cleo is a great teacher!" Oswald said.

25
00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:06.979
"Can you teach us how to lasso?" Nathan asked.

26
00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:11.225
"Sure!" Cleo grabbed her rope.

27
00:02:11.226 --> 00:02:15.127
Now that city cat had been practicing lassoing.

28
00:02:15.128 --> 00:02:19.038
The truth was she was getting pretty darn good.

29
00:02:19.039 --> 00:02:22.358
She didn't mind showing off a bit.

30
00:02:22.359 --> 00:02:25.620
First she lassoed the coat rack.

31
00:02:25.621 --> 00:02:29.257
Next she lassoed the globe.

32
00:02:29.258 --> 00:02:33.435
Then she lassoed the teacher's chair.

33
00:02:33.436 --> 00:02:36.519
The students clapped.

34
00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:40.561
"Deputy, could I please try?" Nathan asked.

35
00:02:40.562 --> 00:02:46.162
"Come on up here, Nathan." Cleo handed him the rope.

36
00:02:46.163 --> 00:02:49.580
"That's right—make a loop with a knot.

37
00:02:49.581 --> 00:02:55.093
Now swing it over your head." Cleo stepped back to watch.

38
00:02:55.094 --> 00:02:58.603
Nathan swung the loop in circles a few times.

39
00:02:58.604 --> 00:03:01.161
Then it sailed through the air.

40
00:03:01.162 --> 00:03:05.196
The lasso slipped right over the deputy's head!

41
00:03:05.197 --> 00:03:08.083
"I did it!" Nathan shouted.

42
00:03:08.084 --> 00:03:10.762
He pulled the rope tight.

43
00:03:10.763 --> 00:03:14.334
The students cheered.

44
00:03:14.335 --> 00:03:18.638
Cleo chuckled. "You got me all right."

45
00:03:18.639 --> 00:03:23.992
Her arms were pinned to her sides. "Now let me go."

46
00:03:23.993 --> 00:03:27.402
"Okay." Nathan kept tugging on the rope.

47
00:03:27.403 --> 00:03:30.992
Then he tried to undo the knot.

48
00:03:30.993 --> 00:03:34.241
But it didn't come loose.

49
00:03:34.242 --> 00:03:44.930
He stared at Cleo. "I . . . I think it's stuck!"

